    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0062",
      "sequence": 917,
      "meaning": "Rāma joyfully embraces Hanumān, ever grateful and all-knowing. The physician immediately applies the remedy; Lakṣmaṇa rises delighted, and Rāma clasps him to his heart as all the bears and monkeys rejoice. Hanumān returns Suṣeṇa exactly as he brought him. Hearing the news, Rāvaṇa beats his head in anguish and wakes Kumbhakarṇa by many devices. The giant rises like embodied Death and asks why his brother’s face is withered. Proud Rāvaṇa relates Sītā’s abduction and the slaughter of his greatest night-rangers—Durmukha, Atikāya, Akampana, Mahodara and other battle-firm heroes. Kumbhakarṇa laments: after abducting the Mother of the world, the fool still desires welfare.",
