    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0063",
      "sequence": 918,
      "meaning": "Kumbhakarṇa says Rāvaṇa acted badly and asks why he was awakened only now. Even now he should abandon pride and worship Rāma. Can Raghunātha be merely human when he has a servant like Hanumān? Rāvaṇa committed grave wrong and should have consulted him before opposing the Lord served by Śiva, Brahmā and the gods. Kumbhakarṇa would have repeated Nārada’s teaching if time had allowed. Now he asks his brother to embrace him and let him make his eyes fruitful by beholding the dark, lotus-eyed remover of the three afflictions. For a moment he is absorbed remembering Rāma’s beauty and virtues. Rāvaṇa orders countless jars of wine and many buffaloes.",
