    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0064",
      "sequence": 919,
      "meaning": "After eating buffaloes and drinking wine, Kumbhakarṇa roars like a thunderbolt and strides alone from the fortress, drunk with battle and leaving the army behind. Vibhīṣaṇa approaches, falls at his feet and names himself. Kumbhakarṇa lifts and embraces his younger brother, pleased to know him Raghupati’s devotee. Vibhīṣaṇa tells how Rāvaṇa kicked him for offering supremely beneficial counsel and how his humility pleased Rāma. Kumbhakarṇa says Rāvaṇa is ruled by Time and will accept no teaching, then repeatedly blesses Vibhīṣaṇa as ornament of the demon line for guilelessly worshipping Rāma, ocean of beauty and joy. He sends him away: unable now to distinguish friend from foe, Kumbhakarṇa too is under Time.",
