    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0065",
      "sequence": 920,
      "meaning": "Vibhīṣaṇa returns to the ornament of the three worlds and warns that mountain-bodied, battle-firm Kumbhakarṇa approaches. Strong monkeys shriek, lift trees and mountains and rain millions of peaks upon him, yet neither mind nor body turns—like an elephant struck by arka fruit. Hanumān’s fist knocks him senseless to earth; rising, he strikes Hanumān down in turn. He dashes Nala and Nīla upon the ground and scatters warriors until the monkey army flees in terror. After felling Aṅgada and others and Sugrīva, the boundless giant tucks the monkey king beneath his arm and carries him away.",
