      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0066",
      "sequence": 921,
      "meaning": "Śiva explains that Raghupati performs human play as Garuḍa toys with gathered serpents; such a battle hardly suits one whose bent brow consumes Time, but it spreads holy fame by which people cross becoming. Hanumān recovers and searches for Sugrīva. The monkey king too awakens; Kumbhakarṇa had considered him dead. Sugrīva bites off his nose and ears and leaps roaring into the sky. Kumbhakarṇa seizes his feet and dashes him down, but he lightly springs up, strikes again and returns victoriously to the Lord. Realizing his mutilation, Kumbhakarṇa turns back in anger and shame. Naturally terrifying, now earless and noseless, he frightens the monkey army, which charges with cries of victory and hurls whole masses of mountains and trees.",
