      "meaning": "Kumbhakarṇa advances furiously into battle like angry Death, seizing and eating millions of monkeys as locusts vanish into a mountain cave. He crushes millions against his body and grinds millions into earth-dust; troops escape through mouth, nose and ear openings. Mad with battle pride, he seems ready to swallow the world, too deaf and blind to heed recall. He tears apart the monkey army as more night-rangers arrive. Seeing his host distressed and enemy forces approaching in many forms, lotus-eyed Rāma tells Sugrīva and Vibhīṣaṇa to steady the army while he tests the villain’s strength.",
