      "meaning": "Raghunātha readies Śārṅga and his quiver and advances to destroy the enemy host. First he twangs the bow, its roar deafening the foe, then true to his vow releases hundreds of thousands of arrows like winged serpents of Death. Innumerable shafts fly everywhere, cutting down dreadful demon warriors: feet, chests, heads and arms are severed, and many heroes fall in a hundred pieces. Wounded champions whirl to earth, regain themselves and fight again; struck like thunderclouds, many roar while others flee the hard arrows. Fierce headless trunks run crying ‘seize, strike.’ In an instant Rāma’s arrows destroy the demons, then all return to Raghubīra’s quiver.",
