      "sequence": 925,
      "meaning": "Bear and monkey hosts flee like flocks of sheep at sight of a wolf, crying in distress that this demon is famine descending upon monkey-land. They plead with Rāma, cloud of mercy and destroyer of the surrendered’s pain. Hearing them, the Lord compassionately readies bow and arrows, sends his army behind and advances in anger. A hundred arrows pierce Kumbhakarṇa, but he charges full of rage and makes the earth reel like a moving mountain. He uproots a peak; Rāma cuts off the arm carrying it. He charges with a mountain in the left arm, which the Lord also severs. Armless, he resembles wingless Mandara and glares as if to swallow the three worlds, then opens his mouth and rushes with a terrible scream while gods and siddhas cry out in fear.",
